# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Commit Message Template — Heart Disease Prediction System
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Format:  <type>: <WHAT changed> — <WHY it was done>
# Max 80 chars ──────────────────────────────────────┤ (this line is 80 chars)
#
# Allowed types:
#   feat      New feature or capability
#   fix       Bug fix or correction
#   refactor  Code restructuring (no behavior change)
#   perf      Performance improvement
#   docs      Documentation only
#   test      Adding or updating tests
#   style     Formatting, linting (no logic change)
#
# Rules:
#   • Explain WHAT was done and WHY it was necessary
#   • Keep the subject line under 80 characters
#   • Use imperative mood ("Add", not "Added")
#   • No vague messages: "update", "changes", "fix stuff"
#
# Examples:
#   feat: Add cardio training pipeline — enable population risk prediction
#   fix: Remove duplicate records before split — prevent data leakage
#   refactor: Centralize model loading — avoid double preprocessing
#   docs: Add experiment comparison notes — clarify dataset differences
#   test: Add artifact existence checks — catch missing model files early
#   perf: Cache singleton model bundle — eliminate repeated disk I/O
#   style: Apply black formatting to ml/ — enforce consistent code style
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

